✨ Overview

Shelby Flash Tool V2.1 focuses on developing a graphical user interface (GUI) for a more organized, user-friendly, and efficient firmware flashing workflow.

The goal is to simplify device operations, improve workflow visibility, and make flashing procedures easier to follow for technicians and advanced Android users.

🆕 Development Highlights

🖥️ GUI Development

- Development of a graphical interface using C#.
- Improved organization of tool controls and operations.
- Focus on a cleaner, more accessible user experience.
- Structured workflow for managing flashing operations.

📱 Flashing Workflow

- Organized workflow for firmware flashing operations.
- Partition selection and management workflow.
- Device operation and reboot workflow.
- Focus on making each operation easier to monitor.

📋 Logs & Operation Status

- Dedicated log-viewing workflow.
- Improved visibility of operation output.
- Easier troubleshooting through operation logs.
- Better separation between flashing operations and their results.

🛠️ Project Structure

- C# project files included for development and maintenance.
- GUI development and tool integration work.
- Focus on maintainability and future improvements.

🔧 Planned Improvements

- Further GUI refinements.
- Improved device detection and status reporting.
- More detailed flashing progress information.
- Better error handling and diagnostic messages.
- Additional workflow improvements based on testing and user feedback.

⚠️ Important Notes

- Features and compatibility must be verified against the actual build.
- Flashing support depends on the device, firmware, drivers, and supported flashing backend.
- Always back up important data before flashing firmware.
- Incorrect firmware or partition selection can cause boot failures or device damage.
- Do not flash critical partitions unless the firmware and device compatibility have been confirmed.

